        "senderName": "NWS Milwaukee/Sullivan WI",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued September 2 at 2:46AM CDT by NWS Milwaukee/Sullivan WI",
        "description": "At 246 AM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nRosendale, or near North Fond Du Lac, moving east at 45 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nFond Du Lac, Southern Lake Winnebago, Taycheedah, Mount Calvary, St.\nCloud, Calvary, Peebles, Marytown, Town of Forest, Johnsburg, and\nPipe.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nU.S. Highway 151 near mile marker 163, and between mile markers 165\nand 169.\nInterstate 41 near mile marker 96.",
        "instruction": "If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.\n\nFrequent cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.\nLightning can strike 10 miles away from a thunderstorm. Seek a safe\nshelter inside a building or vehicle.",
        "response": "Execute",
