        "senderName": "NWS La Crosse WI",
        "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 2 at 2:42AM CDT until September 2 at 3:15AM CDT by NWS La Crosse WI",
        "description": "At 241 AM CDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line\nextending from near Independence to 7 miles northwest of North Bend\nto near Holmen, moving east at 55 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\nThese severe storms will be near...\nWhitehall, Blair, and North Bend around 245 AM CDT.\nSparta, Black River Falls, Alma Center, and Cataract around 300 AM\nCDT.\nMerrillan around 305 AM CDT.\n\nOther locations impacted by these severe thunderstorms include\nFranklin, Shamrock, Camp Decorah, Stevenstown, Perry Creek Recreation\nArea, North Branch, and County Roads D E And E.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 94 between mile markers 97 and 123.\nInterstate 90 in Wisconsin between mile markers 1 and 7, and near\nmile marker 11.",
        "instruction": "For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.",
        "response": "Shelter",
        "note": null,
